# EAS Build upload filter. The build scripts in apps/mobile/package.json run with EAS_NO_VCS=1: in Git mode EAS uploads a
# shallow clone whose .git still holds every tracked screenshot (about 64 MB), so this file alone cannot shrink the upload.
# With EAS_NO_VCS the project is copied from the repo root through this file only (about 3 MB).
# When this file exists EAS ignores .gitignore, so everything .gitignore excludes is repeated here.
# Keep in sync with .gitignore.
node_modules
.expo
dist
*.log
.DS_Store
.remember
.claude
.playwright-mcp
apps/mobile/ios
apps/mobile/android

# personal data exports used to build importers: never upload either
NaturalCycles-*.xlsx

# not needed to build the app (about 125 MB, mostly Maestro screenshots). The app imports copy/ at runtime, so copy/ stays.
docs/
apps/mobile/.maestro/
tools/backtest/proto.py

# EAS_NO_VCS uploads untracked files too, so anything local and private must be listed here (security review)
.superpowers
.git
.env
.env.*
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.mobileprovision
credentials.json
google-services.json
*.xlsx
*.xls
